{
  "dom_id": "step-q129526",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=20$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{Var}[0.5X-2Y].$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[0.5X-2Y]={(0.5)}^{2}\\cdot 20+{(-2)}^{2}\\cdot 5=25.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
